<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estado Novo (Portugal)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Estado Novo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estado Novo ('New State') was the authoritarian regime that ruled Portugal from 1933 to 1974, led for most of that time by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-oliveira-salazar">António de Oliveira Salazar</a>. It insisted on keeping the colonies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> and fought costly colonial wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution">Carnation Revolution</a> of 1974 overthrew it and led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">decolonisation</a>.</p></div>
